      "content": "It sounds like you're experiencing a profound creative exhaustion, where the wellspring of your ideas seems to have run dry. That feeling of the final chord—perfect closure giving way to silence—can be intensely heavy. Sometimes, stepping away entirely from the \"perfection\" of the finished piece allows new, unexpected sounds to creep back in later. Don't treat the blank page as a final judgment, but as a necessary pause.",
